{"id": "b543bcb2-1f3b-4d96-b23f-19e14e297d39", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Your agent space has one account, 012345678901_1. I'm running two checks in parallel: one on configuration and data protection, and one on performance and monitoring.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_BcsKmAfOHMoJYtZVLkgBLh", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only production-readiness audit of EBS CONFIGURATION and DATA PROTECTION in us-east-1.",
  "context": "User has a launch next week and asks 'Is my storage production-ready?'. Produce a concise findings report with severity (High/Med/Low) per finding and concrete counts/IDs. Read-only calls only; do not modify anything.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1"],
  "criteria": "Check: (1) inventory of volumes: count, type (flag gp2 that could be gp3, io1 vs io2, st1/sc1 for boot/latency-sensitive), sizes, IOPS/throughput provisioning, state (flag unattached/'available' volumes, volumes with DeleteOnTermination issues on critical instances), AZ distribution; (2) encryption: unencrypted volumes and snapshots, KMS key type (default aws/ebs vs CMK), and whether EBS encryption-by-default is enabled in the region (get_ebs_encryption_by_default); (3) backups: snapshot coverage per in-use volume (age of most recent snapshot, volumes with no snapshots), Data Lifecycle Manager policies (get_lifecycle_policies) and AWS Backup plans/selections covering EBS, snapshot retention, orphaned/old snapshots, snapshot public sharing, EBS snapshot block public access state, Fast Snapshot Restore usage; (4) Multi-Attach, Recycle Bin rules for snapshots/AMIs, volume modification state (stuck 'optimizing'), tagging consistency (Name/Environment/Owner) on volumes; (5) EC2 instance attachment: is critical instance EBS-optimized, and are instance types' EBS bandwidth limits compatible with attached volume throughput. End with a prioritized list of gaps to fix before launch."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit EBS configuration and backups in us-east-1"}, {"id": "tooluse_EPwXgvSBHl5WTQK35SuU74", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-perf-monitoring", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only review of EBS PERFORMANCE HEADROOM and MONITORING in us-east-1 to judge launch readiness.",
  "context": "User has a launch next week and asks 'Is my storage production-ready?'. A separate agent covers configuration/encryption/backups; do NOT duplicate that. Focus on capacity/performance headroom and alerting. Produce a concise report with severity per finding and concrete volume IDs/values. Read-only only.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/EBS (and CWAgent disk_used_percent if present)"],
  "timeframe": "Last 14 days up to 2026-11-23T19:44:00Z",
  "criteria": "For in-use volumes: (1) peak and p95 IOPS vs provisioned (VolumeReadOps+VolumeWriteOps), throughput vs provisioned (VolumeRead/WriteBytes), VolumeQueueLength, VolumeIdleTime, VolumeThroughputPercentage / VolumeConsumedReadWriteOps for io1/io2, gp2 BurstBalance trending low (<50%) or depleted, VolumeStalledIOCheck/StatusCheckFailed; (2) filesystem usage if CWAgent disk metrics exist (flag >75%); (3) instance-level EBS limits: EBSReadBytes/EBSWriteBytes, EBSIOBalance%/EBSByteBalance% for burstable-EBS instance types; (4) CloudWatch alarms covering EBS/instances (BurstBalance, queue length, status checks, disk usage, idle) - list which exist and which are missing for production volumes, and whether alarms have actions (SNS) configured; (5) any EBS-related AWS Health events or Trusted Advisor-style flags available via describe_events/health API (if permitted). Summarize headroom estimate assuming launch traffic could be 2x current peak. End with prioritized recommendations."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS performance headroom and alarms in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

